  "notes": [
    "Machine CPU is the GetSystemTimes busy share over the workload alone; the session\u0027s start and stop are outside it.",
    "A pair, one trial with the session and one without, ran first and is not kept: it warms the consumer and the workload\u0027s first start.",
    "The session is an owned session enabling Microsoft-Windows-Win32k at its message pump keyword, machine-wide, and its consumer only counts Win32k\u0027s records by when each was raised: this is the cost of collecting the keyword, not of admitting or storing its records, a lower bound on a product capture.",
    "A trial\u0027s records a second are those raised while its workload ran, over its time; the records in the second before it are the machine\u0027s own, its other windows\u0027 messages, as no workload of the trial\u0027s ran then.",
    "A pair\u0027s observed difference is kept signed; its impact, as the product classifies it, is the difference or none, and its regression the slowdown or none.",
    "The workload\u0027s processor time is its coordinator\u0027s, receiver\u0027s and sender\u0027s together, and their console hosts\u0027, user and kernel, read from a job holding the six; the consumer\u0027s is this probe\u0027s own over the trial with the session, less its own over the trial without, the session\u0027s settling before the workload and its draining after it included.",
    "A pair\u0027s attributed impact is the processor time the session added, the workload\u0027s and the consumer\u0027s, over the workload\u0027s time and the machine\u0027s processors: what the busy share measures, without what else the machine ran, and with the consumer\u0027s settling and draining counted against the workload."
  ],
